631
00:50:58,880 --> 00:51:02,720
So the brief version is that you can localize your app into many languages.

632
00:51:02,960 --> 00:51:04,720
And when I say localize, I don't mean the app.

633
00:51:04,960 --> 00:51:08,320
I mean the app metadata, which is that name, subtitle and keyword.

634
00:51:09,200 --> 00:51:20,560
And so, a long, long time ago, some developers were tweaking things and realized that Apple uses the English localization for keywords, but also in the US, Spanish from Mexico.

635
00:51:21,200 --> 00:51:27,600
And what that means is that instead of one set of words, one set of name, subtitle, keyword list, you get two.

636
00:51:27,920 --> 00:51:34,640
So if you're optimizing for or if you're localizing for Spanish, all those keywords would also go into the app store.

637
00:51:34,800 --> 00:51:39,680
So if I'm a Spanish speaker and I search in Spanish, I will find your app, which makes sense.

638
00:51:39,840 --> 00:51:41,680
There's a large population of Spanish speakers.

639
00:51:41,920 --> 00:51:44,080
So the app store wants to be accessible to them.

640
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:47,280
If you're not localizing, you're not going localizing for Spanish, use English in there.

641
00:51:47,840 --> 00:51:53,920
And then you have twice the number of everything, twice the characters for the name, the subtitle and the keyword list.

642
00:51:54,320 --> 00:52:02,160
And fairly recently, we discovered that they extended this list beyond Spanish Mexico to also include Russian and a few other languages.

643
00:52:02,320 --> 00:52:08,400
I have them all listed in an article that I wrote, along with a table for all the other countries in which languages are being used.

644
00:52:08,640 --> 00:52:10,320
So I believe now you have five sets.

645
00:52:10,800 --> 00:52:20,000
The interesting thing to keep in mind is that they're all isolated, meaning where they would combine the name, subtitle and keyword list, they're not going to combine all five of them into one.

646
00:52:20,640 --> 00:52:23,840
They're just going to combine all three into one and have five of those.

647
00:52:24,400 --> 00:52:32,480
So you can share keywords between two different sets, which means you can duplicate between different sets but not duplicate within the set, if that makes sense.

